Approach 2: Better (Linear Queue using Array)
Intuition

Maintain

front
rear

Insertion happens at rear.

Deletion moves front.

No shifting required.

Problem:

Once rear reaches the last index,

remaining free spaces at the beginning cannot be reused.

Java
class MyCircularQueue {

    int[] arr;
    int front;
    int rear;

    public MyCircularQueue(int k) {

        arr = new int[k];
        front = 0;
        rear = -1;
    }

    public boolean enQueue(int value) {

        if (rear == arr.length - 1)
            return false;

        arr[++rear] = value;

        return true;
    }

    public boolean deQueue() {

        if (front > rear)
            return false;

        front++;

        return true;
    }

    public int Front() {

        return front > rear ? -1 : arr[front];
    }

    public int Rear() {

        return front > rear ? -1 : arr[rear];
    }

    public boolean isEmpty() {

        return front > rear;
    }

    public boolean isFull() {

        return rear == arr.length - 1;
    }
}

Complexity
All Operations : O(1)

But

Unused space cannot be reused.

