⭐ Interview Tip

The expected solution is to implement a Circular Queue using an array with three variables: front, rear, and size. The key trick is using modulo arithmetic:

Next Index = (current + 1) % capacity

This allows the queue to wrap around and reuse freed positions instead of wasting space. As a result, all operations (enQueue, deQueue, Front, Rear, isEmpty, isFull) run in O(1) time, making it the optimal implementation.
